# Technical Implementation Report

## 1. Source Input

- Source: Direct dispatch with pre-diagnosed root causes (curl-verified against the live `https://direct.shopaikey.com/v1` endpoint), scoped to `scripts/council/client.mjs` and `scripts/council/tiers.mjs` only. Bug 1 and Bug 2 are code fixes; Bug 3 is explicitly scoped as comment-only (no code fix, no product decision made).
- Approved recommendation: Fix bug 1 (kimi-k3 rejects `temperature` presence) and bug 2 (gpt-5.6-sol streams SSE for non-streaming requests); document bug 3 (glm-5.2 reasoning-token exhaustion) as an unresolved comment only.
- Implementation status: COMPLETED

## 2. Implementation Summary

- **Bug 1 fixed:** Added `MODELS_WITHOUT_TEMPERATURE` (a `Set`) in `tiers.mjs` containing `kimi-k3`, with a comment citing the curl-confirmed 400-regardless-of-value behavior. `chat()` in `client.mjs` now builds `body` without a `temperature` key at all, then conditionally adds it only for models not in that set — the key is omitted from serialization entirely, not set to `undefined`.
- **Bug 2 fixed:** Added `parseSseBody()` in `client.mjs`, which reassembles `data: {...}` SSE chunks (skipping the literal `data: [DONE]` line) into the same `{ choices: [{ message: { content } }], usage, error }` shape the rest of `chat()` already expects. Detection is `rawText.trimStart().startsWith('data:')` OR `content-type` includes `text/event-stream`, checked once at the same point the original single-JSON `JSON.parse` happened — the existing non-SSE path is unchanged (kept as the `else` branch of the same `try`).
- **Bug 3 not fixed (by design):** Added a comment next to the `GLM_5_2` export in `tiers.mjs` documenting the reasoning-token-exhaustion finding (unresolved as of 2026-08-02, do not bump `max_tokens` expecting a different outcome). `glm-5.2` remains in `DEFAULT_PANEL` — no code behavior changed for this model, per instructions.
- What was not implemented: Any fix or `max_tokens` change for glm-5.2 — that's explicitly a product decision reserved for the user, not something to decide while fixing bugs 1/2.
- Why: Bug 3 has no known-good fix (a further `max_tokens=8000` test was inconclusive due to an unrelated transient `HTTP 529`), so per instructions it stays documentation-only.

